  "id": "exc-toolz.dicttoolz-merge_with",
  "image_digest": "sha256:ea390db0b06a75508772ea648c158ae15d4d1ea5b2764103f4ec7f9352f828a5",
  "image_tag": "bench-toolz",
  "instruction": "## Goal\nRestore the original behavior of `toolz.dicttoolz.merge_with` so that it merges multiple dictionaries (or mappings) and applies a given function to the list of values associated with each key.\n\n## Observable behavior\n```python\n>>> from toolz.dicttoolz import merge_with\n>>> merge_with(sum, {1: 1, 2: 2}, {1: 10, 2: 20})\n{1: 11, 2: 22}\n```\n\n```python\n>>> from toolz.curried import merge_with\n>>> merge_with(sum)({1: 1}, {1: 2})\n{1: 3}\n>>> merge_with(sum, [{\"a\": 1}, {\"a\": 2}])\n{\"a\": 3}\n```\n\n## Constraints\n- The public API to preserve is `toolz.dicttoolz.merge_with(func, *dicts, **kwargs)`.\n- Files in scope: `toolz/__init__.py`, `toolz/dicttoolz.py`, `toolz/tests/test_curried.py`, `toolz/tests/test_dicttoolz.py`.\n\n## How success is measured\n```\npython -m pytest -q toolz/tests/test_curried.py::test_merge_with toolz/tests/test_curried.py::test_merge_with_list toolz/tests/test_dicttoolz.py::TestCustomMapping::test_merge_with toolz/tests/test_dicttoolz.py::TestCustomMapping::test_merge_with_iterable_arg toolz/tests/test_dicttoolz.py::TestDefaultDict::test_merge_with toolz/tests/test_dicttoolz.py::TestDefaultDict::test_merge_with_iterable_arg toolz/tests/test_dicttoolz.py::TestDict::test_merge_with toolz/tests/test_dicttoolz.py::TestDict::test_merge_with_iterable_arg toolz/tests/test_dicttoolz.py::test_merge_with_non_dict_mappings\n```",
